{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789028667,"nonce":"+omAaMOrK+5kVQ6yrjAsUHzheDI=","message":"Measured against the design intent, which is that AIR is re-serialized to HL opcodes for the HL OPTIMIZER only -- crates/air/src/v2/serialize.rs, what --emit-optimized produces -- and never on the runtime path.\n\nThe runtime path does it anyway. One AOT build of a three-line program:\n\n    3053  AIR instructions re-serialized into opcodes during code generation\n    4385  total translate_opcode calls\n\nair_emit.rs carries its own private AIR-to-opcode rebuild, air_instr_opcode,\n55 arms, duplicating serialize.rs's job inside the LLVM backend and running it\non every compile. The catch-all arm of translate_air_v2 sends every instruction\nit does not handle -- everything but the five vector ops and Pos -- through it.\n\nThat is the inconsistency to remove: the backend should translate Instr to LLVM\nIR the way cranelift/codegen.rs translates Instr to CLIF, and serialize.rs\nshould be the only AIR-to-opcode converter in the tree, used only by the\noptimizer.\n\nTwo symptoms of the current shape, both already in the code as workarounds:\nFieldGet overwrites lowering.regs[ri] to pass AIR's resolved obj_ty through an\nopcode with no field for it, and SetEnumField fabricates an EnumAlloc because\nthe opcode-era primitive finds the construct by scanning preceding opcodes.","files":null}]}